---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { FALLBACK_ORIGIN, SITE_NAME, absoluteUrl } from "../lib/site";

const origin = Astro.site ?? new URL(FALLBACK_ORIGIN);
const homeUrl = absoluteUrl("/", origin);
const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "WebSite",
      name: SITE_NAME,
      url: homeUrl,
      description:
        "Online Model Cost is an LLM cost calculator for one-call and monthly AI model cost comparison.",
    },
    {
      "@type": "WebApplication",
      name: "Online Model Cost",
      url: homeUrl,
      applicationCategory: "FinanceApplication",
      operatingSystem: "Any",
      offers: {
        "@type": "Offer",
        price: "0",
        priceCurrency: "USD",
      },
      description:
        "Browser LLM cost calculator and AI model price comparison for Claude, GPT, Gemini, and Grok.",
    },
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title="Online Model Cost | LLM cost calculator and AI model price comparison"
  description="Online Model Cost is an LLM cost calculator for one prompt and a monthly bill. Compare AI model cost and LLM price across Claude, GPT, Gemini, and Grok in your browser."
  keywords="online model cost, llm cost calculator, llm cost comparison, llm price comparison, ai model cost comparison, ai model price, openai model price, llm cost optimization"
>
  <main id="main" class="shell">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">LLM cost calculator</p>
      <h1>Online Model Cost.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Price one prompt, then a month of calls. Compare AI model cost for
        Claude, GPT, Gemini, and Grok without uploading the text.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="card-grid">
      <a class="choice-card" href="/token-calculator">
        <h2>Token calculator</h2>
        <p>
          Count characters, words, and tokens for Claude, GPT, Gemini, and Grok.
          GPT uses tiktoken in this tab. The other families are labeled
          estimates. The paste never leaves the browser.
        </p>
        <span class="card-cta">Open the token calculator →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="choice-card" href="/api-cost-calculator">
        <h2>API cost calculator</h2>
        <p>
          Tokens per request, requests per day, and users — scaled to a monthly
          bill. Opens its own page, not a panel on this one.
        </p>
        <span class="card-cta">Open the API cost calculator →</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <article class="prose seo-copy">
      <h2>What Online Model Cost is</h2>
      <p>
        Online Model Cost is a browser set of tools for AI model cost. Use it as
        an LLM cost calculator when you need a number before a prompt ships, and
        again when you need a sketch of a monthly bill. The site does not replace
        a vendor invoice. It prices catalog rates for Claude, GPT, Gemini, and
        Grok so you can run an LLM price check in one place. The prompt stays on
        your device. Currency can display in USD or INR. That choice is not a
        copy of your text.
      </p>

      <h2>LLM price check for one prompt</h2>
      <p>
        The token calculator is the first step in an AI model cost comparison.
        Paste the system message, user turn, or excerpt you would send on one
        call. The page counts characters and words as you type, then prices one
        model per family. GPT tokens use tiktoken in this tab. Claude, Gemini,
        and Grok counts are labeled estimates, not those vendors’ tokenizers.
      </p>
      <p>
        The chart is a one-call LLM price for the prompt. Each bar shows that
        model’s cost and token count. If the number is high, trim repeated
        instructions, drop unused context, or switch to a cheaper model in the
        same family. That is the LLM cost optimization this site can do: see the
        price, then cut the prompt. When you open the monthly calculator from
        that result, input tokens carry over from the GPT count. Output starts
        at zero because there is no reply yet. Type an expected answer length
        if you want completion tokens in the bill.
      </p>

      <h2>LLM cost calculator for a month of calls</h2>
      <p>
        The API cost page is a separate LLM cost calculator for traffic, not a
        second paste box. Enter input and output tokens per request, requests
        per day, users, and days in the month. The same usage is priced for one
        Claude, GPT, Gemini, and Grok model so you get an LLM cost comparison
        as a monthly sketch. Direct visits start empty. Arriving from the token
        page fills the prompt’s token count. Use 1 user if requests per day is
        already a team total. Leave output at 0 to bill the prompt only. The
        figure is for planning, not an invoice and not a live quote from OpenAI,
        Anthropic, Google, or xAI.
      </p>

      <h2>AI model price comparison and catalog rates</h2>
      <p>
        AI model price moves. This site does not scrape a live ticker on every
        view. Catalog input and output rates per million tokens sit on the rates
        page, taken from the OpenRouter public list for the allowlisted models.
        That list is the source for the LLM price comparison in the charts.
        OpenAI model price for the GPT rows follows that catalog, as do the
        other families. A spreadsheet of dollars per million tokens does not
        tell you what your text costs. The token page does. A single-call LLM
        price does not tell you what a launch costs. The monthly calculator
        does, once you add traffic.
      </p>

      <h2>FinOps, attribution, and what this site is not</h2>
      <p>
        Some teams want to track AI model cost attribution in FinOps stacks.
        Online Model Cost does not connect to billing exports, tag traces, or
        allocate spend to services. It is a calculator. You can still take a
        number into the system that does attribution: this prompt is this many
        tokens; this many requests per day is this monthly LLM cost. Prompt-layer
        LLM cost optimization is what this page can do. Warehouse-level
        allocation is not.
      </p>
      <p>
        For a catalog LLM price comparison without a prompt, open
        <a href="/rates">catalog rates</a>. For an LLM price calculator on one
        call, open the <a href="/token-calculator">token calculator</a>. For a
        monthly AI model cost comparison, open the
        <a href="/api-cost-calculator">API cost calculator</a>. All three stay
        in the browser. None of them upload the prompt.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />
</Layout>
